From 286e74e57f4c2fcec033ff6739663744096178c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vbardales <virginie.bardales@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 21:49:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(film): a @film-ticks:N tag that films by game ticks
 instead of the clock

A film is paced by a stopwatch at ten pictures a second, so an effect that
lives one tick in fifteen is caught by chance. @film-ticks:N films the scenario
on its own and takes a picture whenever the tick counter has advanced by N,
read on each rendered frame. FilmTickGate holds that rule in Pickle.Core so it
can be unit tested without the game; the recorder asks it on every frame and
falls back to the clock when the tag is absent.

At normal speed @film-ticks:1 gives one picture per tick. Where several ticks
run between two rendered frames the picture lands on the first frame after the
interval, which the documentation says. The real-seconds cap still applies.

AI-assisted: Claude Code
