+`@film-ticks:N` films on its own and counts in game ticks, not in seconds. Use it when the
+thing you want to see lasts a tick or two: a film paced by the clock catches it only by chance.
+The tick counter is read on each rendered frame, so at normal speed `@film-ticks:1` gives one
+picture per tick. At a speed that runs several ticks between two frames, or without `@watch`,
+a picture lands on the first frame after the interval and cannot show the ticks in between.
+It still stops at `-pickle-max-film-seconds`, counted in real seconds.
+
